current job is seriously harming your mental or physical health, in which case leaving sooner may be worth it.", "Option B\n\nKeeping your current job while searching gives you financial stability and reduces the pressure of having to accept the first opportunity that appears. Since starting over already feels daunting, a steady paycheck and a stronger negotiating position will likely make the transition less stressful, unless your current job is seriously harming your mental or physical health."]}
